You know this robot isn't very different from the one you just trained.

This robot needs to double the first number each time.  It is the 32
in the box all by itself.

Once the robot has doubled the number he can copy the box with that number.
This time it'll be the box with 64 in it.

Have you tried training the robot to join the box with the 64 in it
to the end of the box with the 1, 2, 4, 8, 16 and 32 in it?

The robot is fussy unless you use Dusty to remove some stuff from
his thought bubble.

Did you give the robot the box and wait until he's finished?

If I could move I would make the box like this.  I'd give the robot the box.
I'd have the robot copy the 32 in the first box and drop the copy to
double 32.  Then I'd train the robot to copy the box with the 64 in it
and put the copy down.  I'd get the robot to set down his wand and take
out the box with the 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, and 32 in it and I'd join it to the
box with the 64 in it.  I'd have the robot put the result back and
he's done. I'd give him the box and when Dusty arrives I'd vacuum up the
first 32 and the second box from the box in the robot's thought
bubble. I'd give the robot the box again and wait until he's done.
